entry.summary:
Ever wondered what exactly happens when you run console.log("Hello, World!")? JavaScript doesn't just magically run in your browser. It goes through some phases inside the JavaScript Engine (like Google's V8) before your CPU can understand it. Let's break down this journey from raw text to execution: 👀 Parsing is the process of transforming your raw JavaScript source code into a structured representation that the engine can understand. Lexical Analysis (Tokenization / Scanning) The source code is broken down into small, meaningful chunks called tokens (keywords, identifiers, literals, operators, etc.). Example:
let x = 10;
Tokens generated: let (keyword), x (identifier), = (operator), 10 (literal), ; (punctuation). Syntax Analysis (Building the AST) These tokens are then transfor…
